WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:01.200
It doesn't make any sense

2
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:02.470
but she's gonna make sense.
Okay.

3
00:00:02.470 --> 00:00:03.303
Take a look.

4
00:00:03.303 --> 00:00:04.690
For the the last year and a half,

5
00:00:04.690 --> 00:00:06.970
I've been on a quest to trade a single bobby pin

6
00:00:06.970 --> 00:00:08.260
up until I get to a house.

7
00:00:08.260 --> 00:00:11.250
After 28 trades, and all the ups and downs.

8
00:00:11.250 --> 00:00:12.790
I finally did it.

9
00:00:12.790 --> 00:00:15.703
Okay, we're walking up to it.

10
00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:19.515
This feels so surreal.

11
00:00:19.515 --> 00:00:20.348
(audience cheering)

12
00:00:20.348 --> 00:00:22.060
She got a house?

13
00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:22.893
Wow.

14
00:00:22.893 --> 00:00:27.070
So here to tell this how this insane true story happened

15
00:00:27.070 --> 00:00:29.010
is Demi Skipper.

16
00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:29.984
Demi, hi.

17
00:00:29.984 --> 00:00:30.817
(audience cheering)

18
00:00:30.817 --> 00:00:32.540
Hi guys.

19
00:00:32.540 --> 00:00:33.373
Wow.

20
00:00:35.070 --> 00:00:37.820
Take me back to May, 2020.

21
00:00:37.820 --> 00:00:41.070
Where did this idea and bobby pin come from?

22
00:00:41.070 --> 00:00:42.800
Yes. So May of 2020,

23
00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:45.080
I think like a lot of us, I was sitting in quarantine,

24
00:00:45.080 --> 00:00:47.830 line:15%
watching too much TV and came upon a Ted talk

25
00:00:47.830 --> 00:00:50.170 line:15%
about a guy that had done this 20 years ago.

26
00:00:50.170 --> 00:00:52.160 line:15%
And I looked, and he was the only person.

27
00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:54.410 line:15%
So I knew I had to be the second one to do it.

28
00:00:54.410 --> 00:00:56.910
So I grabbed a bobby pin and then started trading.

29
00:00:57.748 --> 00:00:58.581
What?

30
00:00:58.581 --> 00:00:59.414
What's the step...

31
00:00:59.414 --> 00:01:00.247
What are the steps?
(Drew blabbering)

32
00:01:00.247 --> 00:01:02.080
You start with a bobby pin and a dream for a house.

33
00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:03.370
What do you even do with step one?

34
00:01:03.370 --> 00:01:04.690
So there's the bobby pin.

35
00:01:04.690 --> 00:01:05.580
Then what?

36
00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:06.710
Yes, so great question.

37
00:01:06.710 --> 00:01:08.737
So I looked honestly around my own house and said

38
00:01:08.737 --> 00:01:09.730
"What do I have a lot of?"

39
00:01:09.730 --> 00:01:11.310
I found a pack of bobby pins.

40
00:01:11.310 --> 00:01:12.870
I have them sitting all around my house.

41
00:01:12.870 --> 00:01:14.620
So I took one of those bobby pins

42
00:01:14.620 --> 00:01:16.270
and made my first trade with Abby,

43
00:01:16.270 --> 00:01:17.670
who was someone I did not know,

44
00:01:17.670 --> 00:01:19.260
just random stranger online,

45
00:01:19.260 --> 00:01:20.420
but now we still keep in touch.

46
00:01:20.420 --> 00:01:23.270
So Abby wasn't like, "Why are you trying to hawk

47
00:01:23.270 --> 00:01:24.570
a bobby pin that I could find

48
00:01:24.570 --> 00:01:26.560
in the bottom of my dirty purse?

49
00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:29.330
She instead said like, "I'm intrigued",

50
00:01:29.330 --> 00:01:30.860
and traded a pair of earrings?

51
00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:32.230
Is this correct?

52
00:01:32.230 --> 00:01:35.607
So I knew that she was part of my posse when she said,

53
00:01:35.607 --> 00:01:36.440
"You know what?"

54
00:01:36.440 --> 00:01:37.970
"I will trade you a pair of earrings

55
00:01:37.970 --> 00:01:39.940
I got for my birthday but you have to invite me

56
00:01:39.940 --> 00:01:40.773
to the house at the end."

57
00:01:40.773 --> 00:01:42.360
And I was like, "This girl gets me."

58
00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:43.420
She knows me...

59
00:01:43.420 --> 00:01:45.040
Like this is my person.

60
00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:46.910
So you were transparent

61
00:01:46.910 --> 00:01:50.099
about the building blocks of the mission?

62
00:01:50.099 --> 00:01:50.932
Yes.

63
00:01:50.932 --> 00:01:54.920 line:15%
What an intelligent approach to share the story.

64
00:01:54.920 --> 00:01:57.610 line:15%
'Cause I so believe in a collective experience

65
00:01:57.610 --> 00:02:00.270 line:15%
and I do believe we wanna lift each other up.

66
00:02:00.270 --> 00:02:03.550 line:15%
And you are living proof that that is the case.

67
00:02:03.550 --> 00:02:04.450 line:15%
Yeah, totally.

68
00:02:04.450 --> 00:02:07.957 line:15%
Yes.
(audience applauding)

69
00:02:07.957 --> 00:02:09.160 line:15%
I'm curious though.

70
00:02:09.160 --> 00:02:10.350 line:15%
It took you a year and a half,

71
00:02:10.350 --> 00:02:13.380 line:15%
like what did you end up trading for the house?

72
00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:14.213 line:15%
Great question.

73
00:02:14.213 --> 00:02:15.930 line:15%
So there are 28 trades total.

74
00:02:15.930 --> 00:02:17.510 line:15%
So I did not just go from a bobby pin

75
00:02:17.510 --> 00:02:18.850 line:15%
and then got a house and it was over.

76
00:02:18.850 --> 00:02:20.440 line:15%
There were many ups and downs.

77
00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:25.140 line:15%
My final trade was a $40,000 food truck trailer.

78
00:02:25.140 --> 00:02:28.010 line:15%
So it had solar panels, a battery.

79
00:02:28.010 --> 00:02:28.843 line:15%
So everything you needed

80
00:02:28.843 --> 00:02:31.120 line:15%
to start your own food truck company essentially.

81
00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:33.370 line:15%
And someone traded me that for the house.

82
00:02:33.370 --> 00:02:37.073
Is it true that there was a tractor also at one point?

83
00:02:37.930 --> 00:02:40.330
Oh yes, there were three tractors involved,

84
00:02:40.330 --> 00:02:41.670
which I drove myself.

85
00:02:41.670 --> 00:02:42.930
I've never driven a tractor,

86
00:02:42.930 --> 00:02:45.280
but that tractor was part of the trades.

87
00:02:45.280 --> 00:02:48.090
It then traded for a Chipotle Celebrity card,

88
00:02:48.090 --> 00:02:50.540
which is unlimited Chipotle for a year.

89
00:02:50.540 --> 00:02:51.755
Didn't know what that was.
Now you're talking.

90
00:02:51.755 --> 00:02:52.588
Yeah.
Yeah.

91
00:02:52.588 --> 00:02:55.920
So somebody traded me for a lifetime supply of burritos,

92
00:02:55.920 --> 00:02:59.590
and then she traded for that off-the-grid trailer

93
00:02:59.590 --> 00:03:00.680
that I just told you about.

94
00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:02.090
And then that went to the house.

95
00:03:02.090 --> 00:03:02.990
And just outta curiosity,

96
00:03:02.990 --> 00:03:05.010
where did you park the trailer in the meantime?

97
00:03:05.010 --> 00:03:06.440
Oh, let me tell you.

98
00:03:06.440 --> 00:03:07.400
I live in San Francisco.

99
00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:09.000
I don't have a car of my own.

100
00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:11.080
This was a journey in and of itself-

101
00:03:11.080 --> 00:03:11.913
Oh my God.

102
00:03:11.913 --> 00:03:14.340
San Francisco's the hardest city to park in.

103
00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:15.930
With a a tractor.

104
00:03:15.930 --> 00:03:16.850
Oh, three of them too.

105
00:03:16.850 --> 00:03:18.200
No not one, three.
Oh my...

106
00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:20.390
It's just me walking down the street with three tractors.

107
00:03:20.390 --> 00:03:23.670
So, I found a very gracious friend who had a large garage.

108
00:03:23.670 --> 00:03:26.306
Okay, so I have three rapid fire questions.

109
00:03:26.306 --> 00:03:27.560
Okay.

110
00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:32.560
Are you full of memories now from this journey?

111
00:03:34.350 --> 00:03:37.200
Yes. I mean honestly, I thought that I would trade

112
00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:39.340
a bobby pin for a house and I knew I would get there

113
00:03:39.340 --> 00:03:40.930
even if it took five years.

114
00:03:40.930 --> 00:03:43.480
But you meet so many people along the way.

115
00:03:43.480 --> 00:03:45.390
You end up learning so much about yourself.

116
00:03:45.390 --> 00:03:47.790
It became so much more than just, "Is it possible?"

117
00:03:47.790 --> 00:03:50.330
It became like the people and the memories

118
00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:52.490
of the last two years.

119
00:03:52.490 --> 00:03:56.720
Would you, #2, recommend for someone else

120
00:03:56.720 --> 00:04:01.720
to travel this intricate journey that you've taken?

121
00:04:03.340 --> 00:04:04.173
Absolutely.

122
00:04:04.173 --> 00:04:06.070
I think other people should try it.

123
00:04:06.070 --> 00:04:09.070
I will tell them they will get a hundred no's

124
00:04:09.070 --> 00:04:11.410
on every trade until they get their one yes.

125
00:04:11.410 --> 00:04:13.920
So it's not easy, but they can do it.

126
00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:18.150
And #3, how is your new house?

127
00:04:18.150 --> 00:04:19.760
Oh, it is lovely.

128
00:04:19.760 --> 00:04:24.760
I'm so impressed by you.
(audience applauding)

129
00:04:24.920 --> 00:04:28.170
I am so honored that you would share this story with us

130
00:04:28.170 --> 00:04:33.170 line:15%
because it really is one to wrap your head and heart around.

131
00:04:33.260 --> 00:04:34.750 line:15%
I can't thank you enough.

132
00:04:34.750 --> 00:04:35.583 line:15%
Demi Skipper!
(audience applauding)

133
00:04:35.583 --> 00:04:37.260 line:15%
Well done, Demi.
Thank you for having me.

134
00:04:37.260 --> 00:04:40.955 line:15%
Who tool her life and changed it.

135
00:04:40.955 --> 00:04:42.288 line:15%
And you can too.

136
00:04:43.510 --> 00:04:44.766
Thank you so much.
(audience cheering)

137
00:04:44.766 --> 00:04:47.349 line:15%
(upbeat music)

